  "identity": "Leiden BA-TWS Linguistics, full-time, 180 EC, Dutch and English. The Descriptive Linguistics specialisation is taught in English after the introductory year and remains the neutral selected route.",
  "confirmed": "Year 1 has 25 common EC, the 25 EC English course set, and Quechua plus Word and Meaning as mandatory route preparation. Year 2 has 45 required EC and 15 restricted semester-one EC. Vedic Sanskrit is allowed from Comparative Indo-European Linguistics and its basic reconstruction background is supplied in Year 1. Language and Logic has no entry requirement and is allowed from Language and Cognition. The two are separate from the third-year Digital Text and Data Analysis choice, offered in semester two and open to Humanities students. Fieldwork recommends Speech Sounds of the World, included in the English set. Year 3 confirms Philosophy of Science, Anthropological Linguistics, a 5 EC bound elective, a 10 EC thesis with a separate zero-credit seminar and a 30 EC open elective space. Faculty OER Articles 3.1–3.2 and Appendix B support the curriculum/credit structure and thesis. The programme OER §3.2.9 limits overlap in the Second Language Acquisition minor. The exact thesis seminar requires registration and attendance and covers an independent supervised investigation. These are confirmed course-level requirements, while full cohort progression remains blocked by the repeated Berber slot.",
